This supplementary information is collated from multiple sources and compiled automatically.",,storage,"[experimental] Measurement of trypsin (0.5ng), chymotrypsin (200 ng) and tryptase (100ng) activities. Samples were pretreated at 60°C for 20 minutes. Performed using Trypsin Activity Assay Kit (Fluorometric) protocol. | [experimental] This Trypsin Activity Assay Kit (Fluorometric) provides a simple, rapid way to detect trypsin activity in a wide variety of biological samples. In this kit, trypsin cleaves a synthetic substrate thereby releasing a fluorophore (AMC), which can be easily quantified at Ex/Em = 380/460 nm. By pretreating samples at 60ºC for 20 min, the kit can differentiate the trypsin activity from other structurally similar enzymes such as chymotrypsin and tryptase. The assay is specific, sensitive and can detect as low as 2 µU of trypsin activity in samples.",webpage,https://www.abcam.com/en-us/products/assay-kits/trypsin-activity-assay-kit-fluorometric-ab282916
