SAFETY DATA SHEET,streptavidin,P22629,Thermo Fisher,"The information provided in this Safety Data Sheet is correct to the best of our knowledge, information and belief at the",,"The source reports a buffer/formulation, but its ingredients are not recognized by this simple interpretation rule set. Use the exact composition, pH, concentrations, and manufacturer's technical notes to interpret it. These are general formulation-level interpretations, not proof of the product's stability, biological activity, or suitability for a particular assay.","The information provided in this Safety Data Sheet is correct to the best of our knowledge, information and belief at the",,Not specified,No explicit refrigerated/frozen requirement or interpretable storage temperature was found in the extracted storage evidence.,Delayed and immediate effects as well as chronic effects from short and long-term exposure,"7. Handling and storage | Storage | date of its publication. The information given is designed only as a guidance for safe handling, use, processing, storage,",,,"7. Handling and storage | Storage | Delayed and immediate effects as well as chronic effects from short and long-term exposure | date of its publication. The information given is designed only as a guidance for safe handling, use, processing, storage,","7. Handling and storage | Storage | Delayed and immediate effects as well as chronic effects from short and long-term exposure | date of its publication. The information given is designed only as a guidance for safe handling, use, processing, storage,","2, 3, 4, 6",storage,,PDF,https://assets.thermofisher.com/DirectWebViewer/private/document.aspx?prd=ALFAAJ62428~~PDF~~MTR~~AGHS~~EN~~2020-02-27+11:44:17~~Streptavidin++Streptomyces+avidinii~~
Buffers and stock,thrombin,P00734,Abcam,"Buffers and stock | A collection of 18 recipes, buffers and | Recipes for western blot buffers | Nonidet-P40 (NP-40) buffer | – | Cytoskeletal bound protein extract buffer | Soluble protein buffer | TBS 10X (concentrated Tris-buffered saline) | TBS 10X alternative recipe (concentrated Tris-buffered saline) | TBST (Tris-buffered saline, 0.1% Tween 20) | Medium stripping buffer | Harsh stripping buffer | Bicarbonate/carbonate coating buffer (100 mM) | RIPA buffer | RIPA buffer contains the ionic detergent sodium deoxycholate as an active | extracts. A RIPA buffer gives low background but can denature kinases. It can also | NP-40 buffer | Cytoskeletal bound proteins extract buffer | An alternative recipe for Tris buffer combines Tris base and Tris-HCl. This avoids the | This needs to be done under a fume hood. | To prepare 250 mL stock of buffer A | To prepare 250 mL stock of buffer B",,"Tris/Tris-HCl is a pH-buffering system. The reported pH and concentration are needed to judge the actual formulation. Sodium chloride/saline contributes ionic strength and can affect solubility and protein interactions; its effect depends on concentration and protein properties. A detergent/surfactant may reduce surface adsorption or aggregation in some formulations; the exact purpose and compatibility depend on the specific ingredient and concentration. Bicarbonate can contribute to pH buffering, but its behaviour may depend on the solution's gas exposure and formulation. These are general formulation-level interpretations, not proof of the product's stability, biological activity, or suitability for a particular assay.","Buffers and stock | A collection of 18 recipes, buffers and | Recipes for western blot buffers | Nonidet-P40 (NP-40) buffer | – | Cytoskeletal bound protein extract buffer | Soluble protein buffer | TBS 10X (concentrated Tris-buffered saline) | TBS 10X alternative recipe (concentrated Tris-buffered saline) | TBST (Tris-buffered saline, 0.1% Tween 20) | Medium stripping buffer | Harsh stripping buffer | Bicarbonate/carbonate coating buffer (100 mM) | RIPA buffer | RIPA buffer contains the ionic detergent sodium deoxycholate as an active | extracts. A RIPA buffer gives low background but can denature kinases. It can also | NP-40 buffer | Cytoskeletal bound proteins extract buffer | An alternative recipe for Tris buffer combines Tris base and Tris-HCl. This avoids the | This needs to be done under a fume hood. | To prepare 250 mL stock of buffer A | To prepare 250 mL stock of buffer B",,Not specified,No explicit refrigerated/frozen requirement or interpretable storage temperature was found in the extracted storage evidence.,,,,,,,,storage_information_not_found,Page 3 [handling]: Store in aliquots at -20°C (temperature: -20°C),PDF,https://docs.abcam.com/pdf/protocols/buffer-and-stock-solutions-for-western-blot.pdf
